{
  "package": "net/netip",
  "notes": "Addr is std::net::IpAddr plus an optional zone and delegates zone-free predicates and accessors to std (is_loopback, is_multicast, is_unspecified, to_canonical for Unmap and the canonical forms, Ipv4Addr::is_link_local/is_private/is_broadcast, to_ipv4_mapped for Is4In6, octets, to_bits for Next/Prev); IPv6 link-local unicast, unique-local (private), interface/link-local multicast stay ours because std's versions are unstable, and the Go-only parts (zones, Prefix, text forms) are ours. net::netip is Go's netip: Addr/AddrPort/Prefix value types with Go's exact ParseAddr/ParsePrefix/ParseAddrPort grammar and error texts, zones, IPv4-mapped forms and text/binary codecs, convertible to and from std::net. The zero Addr is Addr::default(). Zones are Rust strings, so non-UTF-8 zone bytes in UnmarshalBinary become U+FFFD; Marshal*/Append* return Result like Go's (T, error); Prefix::bits returns isize (-1 when invalid); As4 panics like Go (and so does Result::unwrap, which MustParse* maps to).",
